rows.en:
In the room where she'd been changing, a bright red wedding dress was lying on the floor.
The one who found the red dress was Sato.
When he ran over to it in shock, the dress just vanished into thin air, or so the story goes.{p}

This is something Sato talked about later...
He said it felt like he heard a voice coming from somewhere.
And the voice said this, apparently.{p}

Hey, {a}.
What do you think that means...?
.........{p}

There was a small trace of blood on the carpet.
"I wonder if this will still work...?"
She snipped off the bloodstained carpet fibers with scissors and tried placing them in the center of the magic circle.{p}

But her hobbies were a bit, well...
Not just a bit, really...
Remember how I told you earlier it's better not to get too into fortune-telling and stuff?{p}

But one day, out of nowhere, her boyfriend started being cold to her.
She was really sad.
So she went to the fortune-telling shop she always went to, to get a reading on what would happen from then on.{p}

"Gyaaaaaaaaah!☆"
A scream rang out from the fortune-telling parlor.
It was Hirai's voice...{p}

There was no sound, but she felt a tiny pop, and a red, bead-like drop spread over her white fingertip.
It fell from her fingertip to the floor, drip, drip.
From where the blood fell, thin wisps of white smoke began to rise, swaying and drifting as if to cling to Hirai's body.{p}

"Oh my, so you want to quit?"
The fortune-teller was still grinning, just as before.
But then that smile slid away, and{p}

"And you said you were prepared.
That won't do at all.
Telling lies like that!"{p}

For a while after that, Hirai went through some painful days.
Why? Because she could hardly ever see Tanaka.
At school, something always got in the way and she couldn't even catch a glimpse of his face, and when she finally got to see him after school, he'd be with his new girlfriend...{p}

There's a better way than casting curses. You'd do better to polish yourself more, she said.
And she promised Hirai she would make her even more beautiful.
To do that, the fortune-teller said, she needed Hirai's nails this time.{p}

She pulled something glinting out of her pocket.
It was a box cutter.
And she slid her arm around Suzuki's back, and from behind...{p}
